// @expect-error A function type's 'throws' list needs the function type in parentheses. Write '(() -> void throws Boom)'.
// @expect-error A function type's 'throws' list needs the function type in parentheses. Write '((int) -> int throws Boom)' to have the returned function throw those types, or '((int) -> int) throws Boom' to have the declaration itself throw them.
// @expect-error This function type is marked 'throws' but lists no exception types. Without a body, the types it throws must be written out. List them after 'throws', as in '(() -> void throws Error)', or remove 'throws'.
// @expect-error A declared throws type must be 'Error' or a subclass of it, and 'Speaker' is neither. Remove 'Speaker' from the 'throws' list, or replace it with a class that extends 'Error'.
// @expect-error The 'throws' list names both 'Error' and 'Boom'. 'Boom' is a subclass of 'Error', so 'Error' alone covers both. Remove 'Boom'.
// @expect-error This lambda can throw 'Other', which the function type it is given to does not list. Add 'Other' to that function type's 'throws' list, or move the throwing code into a named function that catches 'Other' with a 'catch' clause.
// @expect-error This lambda can throw 'Boom', but the function type it is given to has no 'throws' list. Add 'throws Boom' after that function type's return type, as in '(() -> void throws Boom)', or move the throwing code into a named function that catches 'Boom' with a 'catch' clause.
// @expect-error can throw 'Boom'. Prefix it with 'try'
// @expect-error 'try' is not needed here
// @expect-error The default value of parameter 'value' calls the function value 'makeProducer()', which can throw 'Boom'. A default value runs at each call that leaves the argument out, and no 'try' can be written there. Move the call into a function that catches 'Boom' with a 'catch' clause, and call that function here.
// @expect-error The default value of field 'value' calls the function value 'makeProducer()', which can throw 'Boom'. A field default runs as each object is built, where no 'try' can be written. Move the call into a function that catches 'Boom' with a 'catch' clause, and call that function here.
// @expect-error Unknown type 'Bom'. Check the spelling, or import the module that declares it.
// @expect-error Undefined function 'undefinedHelper'. Check the spelling, or import the module that declares it.
// @expect-error build failed with 13 problems
// The rules a function type's throws list answers to, and the 'try' rules a call through the
// value is held to.
class Boom extends Error {
    protected constructor(string message) { super(message); }
}

class Other extends Error {
    protected constructor(string message) { super(message); }
}

interface Speaker {
    speak() -> string;
}

raise() throws Boom {
    throw new Boom("bang");
}

raiseOther() throws Other {
    throw new Other("other");
}

missingParentheses(() -> void throws Boom body) {
    print("refused");
}

// In a return position the same mistake has two plausible meanings, so the error names both
// spellings instead of only the function-type one.
ambiguousReturn() -> (int) -> int throws Boom {
    return (value) -> value;
}

noList((() -> void throws) body) {
    print("refused");
}

notAnError((() -> void throws Speaker) body) {
    print("refused");
}

overlapping((() -> void throws Boom, Error) body) {
    print("refused");
}

takesThrowing((() -> void throws Boom) body) throws Boom {
    try body();
}

takesPlain(() -> void body) {
    body();
}

callWithoutTry((() -> void throws Boom) body) {
    body();
}

tryWithoutThrows(() -> void body) {
    try body();
}

// An entry that does not resolve leaves the thrown types unknown. The 'try' and the 'catch'
// are then not judged.
unresolvedEntry((() -> void throws Bom) body) {
    try body();
} catch (Boom e) {
}

// A call to an undefined function raises unknown types, so the 'try' and the 'catch' are not judged.
undefinedCallee() {
    try undefinedHelper();
} catch (Boom e) {
}

// A default value has nowhere to put a 'try', so a call through a throwing function value is
// refused there.
makeProducer() -> (() -> int throws Boom) {
    return () -> { try raise(); return 1; };
}

defaultCallsThrough(int value = makeProducer()()) {
    print("{value}");
}

class FieldDefault {
    int value = makeProducer()();

    protected constructor();
}

main() -> int {
    // The body raises a type the target does not list.
    try takesThrowing(() -> { try raiseOther(); });
    // The target lists nothing at all.
    takesPlain(() -> { try raise(); });
    return 0;
} catch (Boom e) {
    return 1;
}
